Arc-Gno-Mal-Neu
wishless, genocideless, artiwishless, polypileless

After finishing my alphabetic ascension series earlier this year, I
took a break from playing NetHack. The time was spent exploring DCSS,
but after dying for umpteenth time (the best I could achieve was
clearing Lair, Orcish Mines and Hive with TrBe), I felt urge to play
NetHack again. I decided I will try to do atheist conduct with an
archeologist. After Crawl I had mental image of NetHack as rather easy
game, but I was sadly mistaken. It kept dying time after time and I
couldn't get a good game going.

1) Found helm of telepathy on dlvl 3.

2) In shop on dlvl 2 (to which I returned after acquiring new pet and
some money), there were speed boots on sale.

3) Magic whistle in a dlvl 4 shop.

4) Explored first level of the Gnomish Mines, found bag of holding
there.

5) Continued exploring the main dungon; on Oracle level my cat killed
unicorn, so I could finally replace my pick-axe with better weapon.

6) On the level below Oracle, I got blinded and attacked by gold
golem, that got me down to 1 HP. There was simple choice: break
atheist conduct and pray or die. I decided that this game is too nice
to forfeit and prayed. Bye bye atheist. I started thinking about going
wishless.

7) Did Sokoban, which killed my cat and gave me second bag of holding,
which I stashed.

8) Returned to the Mines, on the second level I found lamp, that
turned out to be magic. The only magic lamp in my game, but I didn't
intend to use the wish anyway).

9) In lower mines I came across bones of Crinkelite, a samurai. The
bones had cloak of magic resistance, a 0:0 magic marker (I never used
it) and ring of free action. Also got mattock from some dwarf.

10) Got mind flayer in lower Mines. His psychic attacks were not
completely non-threatening at 60 maxHP, but I managed to kill him
before he killed me.

11) After getting a luckstone, I upped my luck with a gray unicorn at
Oracle level; then I prayed on coaligned altar at dlvl 10 and got
instantly crowned -- oh well. At least I got Vorpal Blade, which I
used the rest of the game.

12) On dlvl 13 I get ungulfed by air elemental - a mortal danger for
66 HP arc with AC 4. I zapped it with wand of polymorph and it turned
into a trapper -- with me still engulfed by it! But then I got
immediately regurgitated, as I had ring of slow digestion on. That was
lucky.

13) On dlvl 17 there was throne room with white dragon; I used the
white scales to make WDSM -- well, it was the armor I ascended with; I
never got gray or silver dragon scales.

14) After reaching Medusa, I returned to dlvl 10 temple to turn my
money into divine protection. I also held an identification session.

15) During clearing the Castle I reached XL 14. By this time I decided
that I will go for genocideless/wishless conduct, so I bagged the 0:3
wand of wishing and headed to Quest.

16) Quest went all fine until I reached my nemesis. The Minion of
Huhetotl got me to 21 HP with two blows during which I took out potion
of paralysis and ring of free action. So I engraved Elbereth, wielded
potion of paralysis, paralyzed the Minion and then beheaded him with
my Vorpal Blade! BTW, I found my second magic marker on the Quest goal
level.

17) I cleared VoTD and established my stash there, then went to
explore Gehennom. Unfortunately, basic skill in divination was not
enough to cast magic mapping. Found third magic marker on the first
level of Gehennom (very nice for a wishless player).

18) After getting robe, my magic mapping improved a little, so I
started to using (with some luck). After I got skilled at divination,
my magic mapping went right to 0% failure rate with robe!

19) I stoned Vlad with cockatrice corpse, then got alignment penalty
for breaking his statue. Funny. I noticed there's nurse at top of
Vlad's, so I undressed for some dancing. Right when I was naked,
nasties summoning lich generated and put minotaur right next to me,
who almost killed me right away. I had to pray to survive. Very close
call.

20) I skipped Orcus in hope of getting cockatrice in levels below.

21) After reaching VS and dropping the Bell and the Candelabrum on it,
I made a return trip to Itzchak's shop in the Mines to get candles.

22) Then I returned to VotD, made a batch of holy water, potions full
healing (I quaffed 17 to get ~240 maxHP) and finished enchanting my
armor.

23) I cleared Orcus Town and killed Orcus, got 0:5 wand of death, the
only wand of death in my game.

24) Killing Rodney was very straightforward, and so was Moloch's
Sanctum (if little tedious, as levelport in didn't buy me much
advantage).

25) The absolutely horrible part was the run up through Gehennom.
Mysterious force triggered whopping 18 times. Rodney showed up only
once, though.

26) The Planes were nominal, I used Orb of detection to find my way
around (had to recharge it once).

27) On the Astral Plane I revgenocided purple worms twice, broke wand
of teleport to disperse them and went to find the right altar -- which
was the third one.


